Table full name: isb-cgc.TCGA_bioclin_v0.clinical_v1
Column name: case_gdc_id Type: STRING Description: GDC unique identifer for this case; e.g. 7b4ce492-ff40-4bf1-b3e8-75ff83e8746d. This identifier can be used to find more information at the GDC Data Portal ( https://portal.gdc.cancer.gov/cases/7b4ce492-ff40-4bf1-b3e8-75ff83e8746d )
Column name: case_barcode Type: STRING Description: TCGA patient/case barcode; e.g. TCGA-06-0119
Column name: program_name Type: STRING Description: Program Name, always TCGA (The Cancer Genome Atlas) in this table.
Column name: disease_code Type: STRING Description: A code representing the type of cancer. Values can be found at https://gdc.cancer.gov/resources-TCGA-users/TCGA-code-tables/TCGA-study-abbreviations; e.g. OV, GBM, LUAD
Column name: project_short_name Type: STRING Description: Project name abbreviation; the program name appended with a project name abbreviation; e.g. TCGA-OV, etc.
Column name: age_at_diagnosis Type: INT64 Description: Age, in years, at which a condition or disease was first diagnosed
Column name: age_began_smoking_in_years Type: STRING Description: Age, in years, that the participant began smoking
Column name: anatomic_neoplasm_subdivision Type: STRING Description: The spatial location, subdivisions and/or atomic site name of a tumor; e.g. Rectum, Larynx, Tonsil, etc.
Column name: batch_number Type: INT64 Description: The BCR Batch Code; see https://gdc.cancer.gov/resources-TCGA-users/TCGA-code-tables/bcr-batch-codes for explanation of the codes
Column name: bcr Type: STRING Description: Biospecimen Core Resource; e.g. Nationwide Children's Hospital, Washington University
Column name: bmi Type: FLOAT64 Description: Body Mass Index of participant
Column name: clinical_M Type: STRING Description: The clinical M score is a rating of metastasis, that is, how much cancer has spread to distant sites. It is based on results of tests done before surgery, such as physical exams and imaging scans; e.g. MX, M0, M1
Column name: clinical_N Type: STRING Description: The clinical N score is a rating of the extent of cancer within nearby lymph nodes, based on results of tests done before surgery, such as physical exams and imaging scans; e.g. N1, N2, N3
Column name: clinical_stage Type: STRING Description: The stage of the cancer, based on results of tests done before surgery, such as physical exams and imaging scans; e.g. Stage I, Stage II, Stage III, Stage IV
Column name: clinical_T Type: STRING Description: The clinical T score is a rating of the extent of the primary tumor, based on results of tests done before surgery, such as physical exams and imaging scans; e.g. T1, T2, T3, T4
Column name: colorectal_cancer Type: STRING Description: Indicates whether the participant has colorectal cancer; e.g. Yes, No
Column name: country Type: STRING Description: Country of the participant; e.g. Germany, United States, Canada, etc.
Column name: days_to_birth Type: INT64 Description: Days since birth (a negative value, relative to the date of diagnosis which is considered to be t=0)
Column name: days_to_death Type: INT64 Description: If vital_status indicates 'dead', then this is the number of days to death (a positive value) relative to the date of diagnosis.
Column name: days_to_initial_pathologic_diagnosis Type: INT64 Description: The number of days to initial pathologic diagnosis
Column name: days_to_last_followup Type: INT64 Description: If vital_status indicates 'alive', then this is the number of days from the date of diagnosis to the last followup (communication contact).
Column name: days_to_last_known_alive Type: INT64 Description: Number of days from the date of diagnosis to the last day on which a person was known to be alive. This field is a combination of the days_to_last_followup and days_to death fields. Therefore, this field can be used whether the vital_status is 'alive' or 'dead'.
Column name: days_to_submitted_specimen_dx Type: STRING Description: Numeric value to represent the day of the diagnosis for the submitted sample.
Column name: ethnicity Type: STRING Description: The ethnic origination of a participant, independent from race; eg. Not Hispanic or Latino, Hispanic or Latino
Column name: gender Type: STRING Description: Participant gender; e.g. Male, Female
Column name: gleason_score_combined Type: STRING Description: The Gleason Score (ranging from 1 -5) is the grade of the aggressiveness of prostate cancer. The combined Gleason Score is the primary Gleason score  (for the largest area of the tumor) added to the secondary Gleason Score (for the next largest section of the tumor).
Column name: h_pylori_infection Type: STRING Description: Indicator of previous or current diagnosis of Helicobactor pylori infection; e.g. Yes, No, Never, Current
Column name: height Type: INT64 Description: Height of participant in centimeters
Column name: histological_type Type: STRING Description: The histological type of cancer; e.g. Adenosquamous, Astrocytoma, etc.
Column name: history_of_colon_polyps Type: STRING Description: Indicator if the participant had a previous history of colon polyps as noted in the history/physical or previous endoscopic report(s); e.g. Yes, No
Column name: history_of_neoadjuvant_treatment Type: STRING Description: Describes the patient's history of neoadjuvant treatment and the kind of treament given prior to resection of the tumor; e.g. Yes, Pharmaceutical Treatment Prior to Resection, etc.
Column name: hpv_calls Type: STRING Description: HPV strains; e.g. HPV18, HPV45, etc.
Column name: hpv_status Type: STRING Description: Indicates whether the participant has a record of a positive finding for human papillomavirus; e.g. Positive, Negative, Indeterminate
Column name: icd_10 Type: STRING Description: Alphanumeric value used to describe the disease code from the tenth version of the International Classification of Disease (ICD-10)
Column name: icd_o_3_histology Type: STRING Description: Code that represents the histology of the disease using the third edition of the International Classification of Diseases for Oncology, published in 2000, used principally in tumor and cancer registries for coding the site (topography) and the histology (morphology) of neoplasms
Column name: icd_o_3_site Type: STRING Description: Code that represents the site of the disease using the third edition of the International Classification of Diseases for Oncology, published in 2000, used principally in tumor and cancer registries for coding the site (topography) and the histology (morphology) of neoplasms
Column name: lymphatic_invasion Type: STRING Description: Indicator if small or thin-walled vessel invasion is present, indicating lymphatic involvement; e.g. Yes, No
Column name: lymphnodes_examined Type: STRING Description: Indicator whether the lymph nodes were examined; e.g. Yes, No
Column name: lymphovascular_invasion_present Type: STRING Description: Indicator if  invasion of a cancer to the blood vessels and/or lymphatics invasion is present; e.g. Yes, No
Column name: menopause_status Type: STRING Description: A female participant's menopausal status; e.g. Post, Pre, Indeterminate, Peri
Column name: mononucleotide_and_dinucleotide_marker_panel_analysis_status Type: STRING Description: Status of the mononucleotide and dinucleotide marker panel analysis; microsatellite-stable (MSS), low level MSI (MSI-L) if less than 40% of markers were altered and high level MSI (MSI-H) if greater than 40% of markers were altered
Column name: neoplasm_histologic_grade Type: STRING Description: Rating which expresses the degree of abnormality of cancer cells, a measure of differentiation and aggressiveness; e.g. G1, G2, G3, G4
Column name: new_tumor_event_after_initial_treatment Type: BOOL Description: Indicates whether a patient has had a new tumor event after initial treatment; Yes, No
Column name: number_of_lymphnodes_examined Type: INT64 Description: The number of lymph nodes examined 
Column name: number_of_lymphnodes_positive_by_he Type: STRING Description: The number of lymph nodes involved with disease as determined by histological examination
Column name: number_pack_years_smoked Type: INT64 Description: The number of packs smoked per day times the number of years smoked by the participant
Column name: other_dx Type: STRING Description: Indicator and type of other diagnosis; e.g. No; Yes, History of Prior Malignancy; Yes, History of Synchronous/Bilateral Malignancy; Both History of Synchronous/Bilateral and Prior Malignancy
Column name: other_malignancy_anatomic_site Type: STRING Description: The site on the body where the other malignancy occurred; e.g. Bladder, Uterus, etc.
Column name: other_malignancy_histological_type Type: STRING Description: The histological type of cancer of the other malignancy; e.g. Adenosquamous, Astrocytoma, etc.
Column name: other_malignancy_type Type: STRING Description: Indicates whether another malignancy occurred before or at the same time; e.g. Prior Malignancy, Synchronous Malignancy
Column name: pathologic_M Type: STRING Description: The pathologic M score is a rating of metastasis, that is, how much cancer has spread to distant sites. It is based on surgery or biopsy; e.g. MX, M0, M1
Column name: pathologic_N Type: STRING Description: The pathologic N score is a rating of the extent of cancer within nearby lymph nodes, based on surgery or biopsy; e.g. N1, N2, N3
Column name: pathologic_stage Type: STRING Description: The stage of the cancer, based on surgery or biopsy; e.g. Stage I, Stage II, Stage III, Stage IV
Column name: pathologic_T Type: STRING Description: The pathologic T score is a rating of the extent of the primary tumor, based on surgery or biopsy; e.g. T1, T2, T3, T4
Column name: person_neoplasm_cancer_status Type: STRING Description: The participant's cancer status; e.g. With Tumor, Tumor Free
Column name: pregnancies Type: STRING Description: The number of times (including currently if it applies) that a female participant has been pregnant, regardless of outcome.
Column name: primary_neoplasm_melanoma_dx Type: STRING Description: Indicates whether a person had a primary diagnosis of melanoma; e.g. Yes, No
Column name: primary_therapy_outcome_success Type: STRING Description: Kind of outcome achieved after the completion of the initial course of treatment; e.g. Complete Remission/Response, Progressive Disease, etc.
Column name: psa_value Type: STRING Description: A male participant's Prostrate-Specific Antigen (PSA) value
Column name: race Type: STRING Description: The race of a participant, independent from ethnicity; e.g. White, Black or African American, Asian, Native Hawaiian or other Pacific Islander, American Indian or Alaska Native
Column name: residual_tumor Type: STRING Description: Status of the tissue margin following surgical resection; e.g. R0, R1, R2, RX
Column name: stopped_smoking_year Type: INT64 Description: Four-digit year that the participant stopped smoking; e.g. 2010
Column name: tobacco_smoking_history Type: INT64 Description: Category describing current smoking status and smoking history as self-reported by a participant.; e.g. 1, 2, etc.
Column name: tss_code Type: STRING Description: Tissue Source Site Code; see https://gdc.cancer.gov/resources-TCGA-users/TCGA-code-tables/tissue-source-site-codes for explanation of codes
Column name: tumor_tissue_site Type: STRING Description: The location on the body where the tumor exists; e.g. Brain, Ovary, Lung, etc.
Column name: tumor_type Type: STRING Description: Tumor Type; e.g. Primary, Type 1, Type 2
Column name: venous_invasion Type: STRING Description: Indicator if large vessel or venous invasion was detected by surgery or presence in a tumor specimen; e.g. Yes, No
Column name: vital_status Type: STRING Description: Survival state of the participant; e.g. dead, alive
Column name: weight Type: INT64 Description: Weight of participant in kilograms
Column name: year_of_diagnosis Type: INT64 Description: Four digit year of the diagnosis
Column name: year_of_tobacco_smoking_onset Type: INT64 Description: Four-digit year that the participant started smoking; e.g. 2010
Sample rows:
[{'case_gdc_id': '8fb406e7-49b1-4662-860c-5a4d32b9d19c', 'case_barcode': 'TCGA-2G-AALX', 'program_name': 'TCGA', 'disease_code': 'TGCT', 'project_short_name': 'TCGA-TGCT', 'age_at_diagnosis': None, 'age_began_smoking_in_years': None, 'anatomic_neoplasm_subdivision': None, 'batch_number': None, 'bcr': None, 'bmi': nan, 'clinical_M': None, 'clinical_N': None, 'clinical_stage': None, 'clinical_T': None, 'colorectal_cancer': None, 'country': None, 'days_to_birth': None, 'days_to_death': None, 'days_to_initial_pathologic_diagnosis': None, 'days_to_last_followup': None, 'days_to_last_known_alive': None, 'days_to_submitted_specimen_dx': None, 'ethnicity': None, 'gender': None, 'gleason_score_combined': None, 'h_pylori_infection': None, 'height': None, 'histological_type': None, 'history_of_colon_polyps': None, 'history_of_neoadjuvant_treatment': None, 'hpv_calls': None, 'hpv_status': None, 'icd_10': None, 'icd_o_3_histology': None, 'icd_o_3_site': None, 'lymphatic_invasion': None, 'lymphnodes


