Table full name: isb-cgc.TCGA_bioclin_v0.Biospecimen
Column name: sample_barcode Type: STRING Description: TCGA sample_barcode; e.g. TCGA-AB-2809-03A.
Column name: sample_gdc_id Type: STRING Description: Unique GDC identifier for this sample (corresponds to the sample_barcode), eg a1ec9279-c1a6-4e58-97ed-9ec1f36187c5  --  this can be used to access more information from the GDC data portal
Column name: case_barcode Type: STRING Description: TCGA patient/case barcode, eg TCGA-AB-2809 (the first 12 characters of the 16-character sample barcode)
Column name: case_gdc_id Type: STRING Description: GDC unique identifer for this case; e.g. 7b4ce492-ff40-4bf1-b3e8-75ff83e8746d. This identifier can be used to find more information at the GDC Data Portal ( https://portal.gdc.cancer.gov/cases/7b4ce492-ff40-4bf1-b3e8-75ff83e8746d )
Column name: sample_type Type: STRING Description: Two-digit sample_type code which forms part of the sample barcode e.g. 01,11,06, etc.
Column name: sample_type_name Type: STRING Description: The longer name of the sample type; e.g. Primary Tumor, Recurrent Tumor, etc.
Column name: program_name Type: STRING Description: Program Name, always TCGA (The Cancer Genome Atlas) in this table.
Column name: project_short_name Type: STRING Description: Project name abbreviation; the program name appended with a project name abbreviation; e.g. TCGA-OV, etc.
Column name: batch_number Type: INT64 Description: The BCR Batch Code; see https://gdc.cancer.gov/resources-TCGA-users/TCGA-code-tables/bcr-batch-codes for explanation of the codes
Column name: bcr Type: STRING Description: Biospecimen Core Resource; e.g. Nationwide Children's Hospital, Washington University
Column name: days_to_collection Type: FLOAT64 Description: Time interval from the date of biospecimen collection to the date of initial pathologic diagnosis, represented as a calculated number of days.
Column name: days_to_sample_procurement Type: FLOAT64 Description: The number of days from the date the patient was diagnosed to the date of the procedure that produced the sample.
Column name: is_ffpe Type: STRING Description: Indicator to signify whether or not the tissue sample was fixed in formalin and embedded in paraffin (FFPE); almost always NO -- only a few (99) FFPE samples were included in the TCGA project
Column name: num_portions Type: INT64 Description: In some cases, a sample was divided into multiple portions -- up to 6 portions, but for most samples the number is 1 (or even 0).
Column name: num_slides Type: INT64 Description: In some cases, portions of a sample were placed onto multiple slides -- generally not more than 2, but occasionally more.
Column name: avg_percent_lymphocyte_infiltration Type: FLOAT64 Description: The average percentage of infiltration by lymphocytes in a sample or specimen
Column name: avg_percent_monocyte_infiltration Type: FLOAT64 Description: The average percentage of infiltration by monocyte in a sample or specimen
Column name: avg_percent_necrosis Type: FLOAT64 Description: The average percentage of necrosis in a sample or specimen
Column name: avg_percent_neutrophil_infiltration Type: FLOAT64 Description: The average percentage of neutrophil infiltration in a sample or specimen
Column name: avg_percent_normal_cells Type: FLOAT64 Description: The average percentage of normal cells in a sample or specimen
Column name: avg_percent_stromal_cells Type: FLOAT64 Description: The average percentage of stromal cells in a sample or specimen
Column name: avg_percent_tumor_cells Type: FLOAT64 Description: The average percentage of tumor cells in a sample or specimen
